PyMuPDF (imported as `fitz`) is used only in the PDF I/O layer. Exactly two files import
it, and nothing else in the codebase touches it:

  pxrd_review/cell_lambda_check.py    text extraction  (_pdf_text_fitz)
  pxrd_review/gui/_pdf_worker.py      page render + text, in an isolated subprocess

The GUI (pxrd_review/gui/review_gui.py) never imports fitz itself; it routes its PDF
reads through that worker. Swapping the renderer is therefore a change to those two files.

  - Private/personal use and local single-user runs trigger NO AGPL obligations.
