    (AGPL-3.0 sec. 13), brings the AGPL source-availability obligations into play
    for the PyMuPDF portion. A proprietary/commercial product therefore needs
    either (a) Artifex's commercial PyMuPDF license, or (b) a swap to a
    permissively-licensed renderer (e.g. pypdfium2, Apache/BSD-style), which the
    isolated PDF layer makes a contained change.

Data & provenance
-----------------
- No ICDD data is bundled or redistributed. No entry .docx/.dft files and no source
  papers (.pdf) are included. The regression fixtures are a private, external set
  (resolved via $PXRD_REGRESSION_DIR); regression_check.py refuses to run without them.
- The reference tables encode standard crystallographic conventions (controlled
  vocabularies, the Kβ-filter-by-anode rule, monochromator materials, …), hand-curated.
  They do not embed proprietary ICDD field values.
- Check rules were informed by the reviewer's own past review comments and validated
  against a private set of already-corrected entries the author had legitimate access
  to as a Task Group member.
- Entry identifiers appearing in the tests and README are bare ids used to pin
  regression cases; the underlying files are not included and the ids carry no
  proprietary field data.
- The tool operates on the reviewer's own working copies and never modifies source files.

